terms=''.join([
'<p class="muted">Version '+TERMS_VERSION+' · Last updated: '+UPDATED+'</p>',
P('1. Agreement and acceptance','These Terms are an agreement between you and '+ENTITY_TODAY+' You accept these Terms by checking the acceptance box before you submit our questionnaire, on behalf of yourself and the business you represent. If you buy PlainWarden Year One, you also give the separate renewal consent described in section 7. Our <a href="privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle information; it is a notice, not part of this agreement. Contact: '+E+'.'),
P('2. What PlainWarden does','PlainWarden is documentation software for tax, accounting and similar firms. You answer a questionnaire about your practice, and the software assembles a Written Information Security Plan ("Plan") from pre-written content. The Plan records the practices you report, identifies potential gaps and items to confirm, and provides generally applicable compliance-support information with regulatory references. Depending on what you buy, the Service also includes the subscription features listed in section 6 (together, the "Service").'),
P('3. What PlainWarden is not','PlainWarden is not a law firm, accounting firm or security consultant, and the Service is not legal, tax or professional advice. It does not audit, inspect or verify your systems, and it does not determine whether your firm satisfies the FTC Safeguards Rule, IRS requirements, state law or any other rule. Completing or adopting a Plan does not establish compliance or prevent security incidents. Where a situation is legally uncertain, the Plan refers you to a qualified adviser.'),
P('4. Responsibilities','<strong>Yours:</strong> giving accurate and complete answers; reviewing the Plan and correcting anything inaccurate before you adopt it; implementing and maintaining your security program; keeping your Plan current; and deciding when to get advice from a lawyer or security professional. <strong>Ours:</strong> generating the Plan as our software and content are designed to, maintaining our regulatory content through a documented review process, and telling active customers if we find a material error in content used in their Plan. Each Plan shows the date and content version used to prepare it.'),
P('5. What not to send us',"Do not enter client names, Social Security or taxpayer ID numbers, account numbers, passwords or other client personal information in the questionnaire or in messages to us. The Service does not need it. If you send it anyway, we will delete it when we find it."),
'<h2>6. Products and prices</h2><ul><li><em>PlainWarden Plan:</em> a one-time purchase of one Plan for $89.</li><li><em>PlainWarden Year One:</em> an annual subscription costing $149 (an introductory price) for the first twelve months, beginning on the purchase date. Unless you cancel, it renews for successive twelve-month periods at $199 per year (see section 7). It includes the Plan and the services below.</li></ul><p><strong>Available from purchase, for as long as your subscription is active:</strong></p><ul><li><em>Your Plan</em> in Word and PDF, emailed at purchase.</li><li><em>Portal and action-item tracker:</em> track the gaps and items to confirm in your Plan. The tracker records what you enter; we do not verify it.</li><li><em>Staff security training</em> for any number of your staff, with completion records (name, date, score and acknowledgment). Staff can retake it at any time. It does not provide continuing-education credit.</li><li><em>How-to guides</em> for common fixes.</li><li><em>Vendor tracker:</em> a list of your service providers and your review notes, which you maintain. It is not an independent assessment of any vendor.</li><li><em>Audit binder:</em> on request, a PDF emailed to you that compiles your action-item status, training records, vendor records and activity log. It organizes your own records; it is not an audit, assurance report or certification.</li><li><em>Plan updates:</em> report a change in your practice through the portal as often as you need; we email you an updated Plan within 5 business days of each report.</li><li><em>Annual re-review:</em> once in each subscription year, at any time, you can re-answer the questionnaire and receive a regenerated Plan based on your updated answers and our then-current content. It is not an independent legal or security assessment.</li></ul><p><strong>Scheduled emails while your subscription is active:</strong> a reminder at most once a week when action items are overdue or due within 14 days; a vendor check-in on the 5th of January, April, July and October; and a re-review reminder each October 1, before PTIN renewal season.</p><p><strong>Support:</strong> email '+E+'. We reply within 2 business days (Monday to Friday, excluding US federal holidays).</p><ul><li>Prices are in US dollars. Any sales tax we are required to collect is shown at checkout before you pay. We may improve the Service, but we will not remove a service listed above during a period you have paid for without refunding the unused part of that period.</li></ul>',
P('7. Automatic renewal (Year One)','Before you buy Year One, we show the introductory price, the renewal price, the renewal date and how to cancel, and you must check a separate box agreeing to automatic renewal. We record that consent. After purchase we email you a confirmation of these terms. After the first twelve months, your subscription renews each year on the purchase anniversary at $199, charged to your payment method on file, until you cancel. We will not charge a different renewal price unless you affirmatively agree to it before that renewal; a price change never affects a period you have already paid for. We email you 15 to 45 days before each renewal with the amount, the date and how to cancel.'),
P('8. Cancellation','You can cancel automatic renewal at any time online through the "Manage subscription" link in your portal and renewal emails, or by emailing '+E+'. No particular subject line or wording is required, and cancellation does not need our approval. Your cancellation stops future renewal charges as soon as you submit it, and we confirm it by email. Unless you receive a refund that ends your subscription, you keep access through the end of the period you have paid for, and you keep every Plan already delivered. Refunds are covered in the <a href="refunds.html">Refund Policy</a>.'),
P('9. License to your Plan','Once you have paid, we grant you a perpetual license to use, copy and edit each Plan delivered to you for your own business, and to share it with your staff, auditors, insurers, regulators and professional advisers. The questionnaire, software, templates and pre-written content remain ours; you may not resell them or use them to build a competing product.'),
P('10. Acceptable use',"Don't misuse the Service, interfere with it, access it by automated means beyond normal use, or use it for anyone other than your own business without our permission."),
P('11. Warranties','Except as these Terms expressly state, and to the extent the law allows, the Service and Plans are provided "as is," and we disclaim implied warranties, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. This does not limit any right you have that cannot be waived by law.'),
P('12. Limitation of liability','To the extent the law allows, and whether a claim is based on contract, tort (including negligence), statute or any other theory: (a) neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits or revenue; and (b) our total liability for all claims relating to the Service is limited to the greater of the amounts you paid us in the 12 months before the claim arose and the amount you paid for the purchase the claim relates to. These limits do not apply to liability that cannot be limited by law, including liability for fraud, willful injury or violation of law (California Civil Code §1668), or to your payment obligations. The limit also does not reduce our obligation to issue refunds that these Terms or applicable law require.'),
P('13. Indemnity','You will defend and indemnify PlainWarden against third-party claims to the extent they arise from your material breach of these Terms, your unlawful conduct, or information you knowingly submitted that was false. This does not cover claims to the extent caused by our negligence, misconduct or breach of these Terms. We will promptly notify you of any such claim, let you control its defense and settlement (but you may not settle in a way that admits fault for us or imposes obligations on us without our written consent), and reasonably cooperate at your expense.'),
P('14. Changes','We may update these Terms. We email active customers at least 30 days before a material change takes effect. Material changes apply to purchases and renewals made after their effective date; they do not change the terms of a period you have already paid for or affect claims or rights that arose before the change. A change that requires your affirmative consent will not apply to you unless you give it. If a change is required by law during your current term, we will tell you what changed and why, and you may cancel and receive a refund of the unused part of that term.'),
P('15. Disputes','Before starting a lawsuit, either party will send the other a written description of the dispute and try in good faith to resolve it for 30 days. Either party may seek urgent court relief at any time. California law governs these Terms, and disputes will be resolved in the state or federal courts in San Diego County, California, which both parties consent to.'),
P('16. Contact',E)])
